  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask with education",
   "texto": [
    "**Vorrei…** is used to order (want to). It is also worth **Prendo…** (tomo-o).",
    "The waiter asks **Desidera?** (what do you want?) and then **Altro?** (anything else?). When serving you, says **Ecco** (here you are).",
    "To pay: **Quant'è?** (what is it?) and **Il conto, per favore** (the account, please). **Euro** does not change to plural: **nove euro**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "In the Italian bar",
   "texto": [
    "In Italy the «bar» is a cafe. **Un caffè** is a single and short coffee. **Un cornetto** is a cruasan. **Un panino** is a snack.",
    "The quantities carry **di**: **un bicchiere di latte** (a glass of milk), **una tazza di tè** (a cup of tea), **una bottiglia d'acqua** (a bottle of water). In front of vowel, **di** becomes **d'**.",
    "The ingredients are said with **al** or **alla**: **un panino al formaggio**.",
    "**Senza** = no."
   ]
  },
